Oh, no. Niccolo.

1491
00:57:48,381 --> 00:57:49,924
It was an accident, I swear.

1492
00:57:50,008 --> 00:57:51,468
I don't know how it happened.

1493
00:57:51,551 --> 00:57:54,137
-I'm so, so, so sorry.
-You.

1494
00:57:54,220 --> 00:57:57,515
You know what?
I can cause accidents, too.

1495
00:57:57,599 --> 00:57:59,559
Get ready to burn in...

1496
00:57:59,642 --> 00:58:01,019
Oh!

1497
00:58:01,102 --> 00:58:03,271
You mess with my show,
you're gonna get burned.

1498
00:58:03,354 --> 00:58:04,814
Literally.

1499
00:58:09,235 --> 00:58:11,279
That's the
Fontaine 3XL, isn't it?

1500
00:58:11,362 --> 00:58:13,156
Yes. They are.

1501
00:58:13,239 --> 00:58:16,159
You know, they say that dog
is a man's best friend? Yeah?

1502
00:58:16,242 --> 00:58:17,869
- Yeah.
- I say this, too,

1503
00:58:17,952 --> 00:58:20,497
but this curling iron is also
a very good friend of...

1504
00:58:20,580 --> 00:58:22,415
Oh!

1505
00:58:22,499 --> 00:58:24,334
Oh!

1506
00:58:25,668 --> 00:58:27,170
Give me that.

1507
00:58:30,256 --> 00:58:31,966
Go, go, go! Let's go!

1508
00:58:33,801 --> 00:58:34,969
Hey, sorry, we got
held up a little bit...

1509
00:58:35,053 --> 00:58:36,095
Whoa. Oh.

1510
00:58:38,014 --> 00:58:39,974
This is a classic case
of two guys on the ground.

1511
00:58:53,196 --> 00:58:55,698
Where are we? Who are you?
What do you want from us?

1512
00:58:55,782 --> 00:58:56,950
Wait. No, no, no.
Please, come back.

1513
00:58:57,033 --> 00:58:57,992
No, no, no, come back.
Come back!

1514
00:58:58,076 --> 00:58:59,536
Come back!

1515
00:59:00,578 --> 00:59:01,955
What, are they gonna kill us?

1516
00:59:02,038 --> 00:59:03,039
I don't know.
I don't want to die.

1517
00:59:03,122 --> 00:59:04,374
Me neither.

1518
00:59:05,291 --> 00:59:06,918
Wait. Otto.

1519
00:59:07,001 --> 00:59:08,503
Yeah?

1520
00:59:08,586 --> 00:59:10,505
I just remembered...

1521
00:59:10,588 --> 00:59:13,174
-I can pop my ankle out.
-Huh?

1522
00:59:13,258 --> 00:59:15,051
-Okay, do it. Do it.
-Okay.

1523
00:59:16,511 --> 00:59:18,221
Did you do it?

1524
00:59:18,304 --> 00:59:19,430
Yeah.

1525
00:59:21,099 --> 00:59:22,225
But it didn't
achieve anything,

1526
00:59:22,308 --> 00:59:23,059
so I'm gonna pop it
back in, okay?

1527
00:59:23,142 --> 00:59:24,310
Okay. Yeah.

1528
00:59:24,394 --> 00:59:25,436
-Pop it back in. Do it.
-It hurts.

1529
00:59:25,520 --> 00:59:26,771
Ow.

1530
00:59:28,064 --> 00:59:29,440
Oh, Gail.

1531
00:59:29,524 --> 00:59:30,733
I'm so sorry I talked you

1532
00:59:30,817 --> 00:59:31,943
into coming to
Los Angeles with me.

1533
00:59:32,026 --> 00:59:33,778
Otto, don't do that.

1534
00:59:33,861 --> 00:59:38,408
You've been my most consistent,
my most... loving, loyal friend

1535
00:59:38,491 --> 00:59:41,786
ever since my parents'
double suicide.

1536
00:59:41,869 --> 00:59:43,580
And as I've said to
you before, you know,

1537
00:59:43,663 --> 00:59:45,206
I could never presume
to understand

1538
00:59:45,290 --> 00:59:46,833
what it is you've gone through.

1539
00:59:46,916 --> 00:59:48,293
I mean, to find
your mother and father

1540
00:59:48,376 --> 00:59:50,295
in your bed like that.

1541
00:59:50,378 --> 00:59:52,672
-And on your birthday, no less.
-Yeah.

1542
00:59:52,755 --> 00:59:56,426
But all I can do is
be your friend.

1543
00:59:57,468 --> 00:59:58,511
No matter what.

1544
00:59:59,220 --> 01:00:01,055
Until the end.

1545
01:00:03,182 --> 01:00:04,892
Gail Daughtry.

1546
01:00:04,976 --> 01:00:06,811
Hairdresser.

1547
01:00:06,894 --> 01:00:08,479
Finally, we meet.

1548
01:00:08,563 --> 01:00:13,192
Flawless face to flawless face.

1549
01:00:14,360 --> 01:00:15,445
Who are you?

1550
01:00:16,237 --> 01:00:17,739
Where are we?

1551
01:00:17,822 --> 01:00:20,158
Perhaps you
recognize this saloon

1552
01:00:20,241 --> 01:00:23,119
from the movie
Blood on the Wagon.

1553
01:00:23,202 --> 01:00:24,704
I'm sorry, I don't.

1554
01:00:24,787 --> 01:00:26,706
I'm more into, like,
black-and-white Holocaust shit.

1555
01:00:26,789 --> 01:00:28,124
Abandoned years ago.

1556
01:00:28,207 --> 01:00:30,668
A ghost town movie set.

1557
01:00:30,752 --> 01:00:34,839
The irony of building
the New World financial order

1558
01:00:34,922 --> 01:00:39,135
from the ruins of
fake American mythology

1559
01:00:39,218 --> 01:00:41,638
makes me so hard.

1560
01:00:41,721 --> 01:00:45,224
At first, I thought you were
a hired operative.

1561
01:00:45,308 --> 01:00:47,060
-But no.
-Mm-mmm.

1562
01:00:47,143 --> 01:00:50,897
You are just a girl from Kansas
that showed up in my city

1563
01:00:50,980 --> 01:00:52,899
trying to do
I don't know what.

1564
01:00:52,982 --> 01:00:54,484
Have sex with Jon Hamm.

1565
01:00:54,567 --> 01:00:56,277
Oh, like a celebrity pass thing?

1566
01:00:56,361 --> 01:00:57,987
- Exactly.
- Good luck with that.

1567
01:00:58,071 --> 01:00:59,405
Oh, thank you.

1568
01:00:59,489 --> 01:01:00,698
Thank you so much.

1569
01:01:00,782 --> 01:01:01,991
-Kill her.
-Mm-hmm.

1570
01:01:02,075 --> 01:01:05,203
Wait, what?
What did she just say?

1571
01:01:05,286 --> 01:01:08,498
-And her little friend, too.
-No, no, no, no, no, please.

1572
01:01:08,581 --> 01:01:10,041
- Let's do this.
- Please, not Otto!

1573
01:01:16,964 --> 01:01:18,341
Stop!

1574
01:01:19,467 --> 01:01:21,511
Who the fuck
is Remy Fontaine?

1575
01:01:25,807 --> 01:01:28,976
He's king of
the whip curl.

1576
01:01:29,060 --> 01:01:30,603
And then, I said to him,

1577
01:01:30,687 --> 01:01:33,523
"Uh, if you mess with my show,
you're gonna get burned.

1578
01:01:33,606 --> 01:01:34,899
"Uh, literally." It just...

1579
01:01:34,982 --> 01:01:37,735
It just seemed like
something to say.

1580
01:01:37,819 --> 01:01:40,071
A catchphrase.

1581
01:01:40,154 --> 01:01:41,781
Hello?

1582
01:01:41,864 --> 01:01:44,492
Your friends tell me you have
something that is mine.

1583
01:01:44,575 --> 01:01:46,202
Who is this? What friends?

1584
01:01:46,285 --> 01:01:49,622
Is this like camp friends?
Is this Lieberman?

1585
01:01:49,706 --> 01:01:51,457
Caleb, do whatever she says.
She's gonna kill us.

1586
01:01:51,541 --> 01:01:53,793
Lieberman, I swear to God,
if this is one of your bits

1587
01:01:53,876 --> 01:01:55,962
it's not even that funny because
I actually have some friends

1588
01:01:56,045 --> 01:01:56,838
who are in legitimate
danger right now.

1589
01:01:56,921 --> 01:01:59,382
Caleb, it's Gail!

1590
01:01:59,465 --> 01:02:03,177
Bring my reports to 25933

1591
01:02:03,261 --> 01:02:04,804
Sand Canyon Way,

1592
01:02:04,887 --> 01:02:09,684
Santa Clarita,
California, 91387.

1593
01:02:09,767 --> 01:02:11,978
And bring them within the hour.

1594
01:02:12,061 --> 01:02:14,731
If not, your friends will die!

1595
01:02:16,858 --> 01:02:20,153
Well, either Lieberman's
upped his game dramatically,

1596
01:02:20,236 --> 01:02:22,989
or Gail and Otto are in
really significant danger.

1597
01:02:23,072 --> 01:02:25,283
-We have to go to that address.
-Hey, wait.

1598
01:02:25,366 --> 01:02:26,743
Who are we kidding?

1599
01:02:26,826 --> 01:02:28,828
They're not gonna let us
just stroll in there,

1600
01:02:28,911 --> 01:02:30,997
save our friends,
and then stroll right back out.

1601
01:02:31,080 --> 01:02:33,875
Come on, let's face it.
They're...

1602
01:02:33,958 --> 01:02:35,168
They're dead already.

1603
01:02:37,295 --> 01:02:38,755
- Vincent.
- Hey, hey, hey.

1604
01:02:39,839 --> 01:02:41,132
Why is this here?

1605
01:02:41,215 --> 01:02:43,760
It's just
a roll of film, man.

1606
01:02:43,843 --> 01:02:46,262
-Why is this in here?
-It's just a roll of film.

1607
01:02:46,345 --> 01:02:48,055
-Why is this in here?
-It's a roll of film!

1608
01:02:48,139 --> 01:02:49,974
-Why is it in here?
-It is a roll of film!

1609
01:02:50,057 --> 01:02:51,809
-Vincent!
-Okay, it's there to remind me

1610
01:02:51,893 --> 01:02:54,061
to never leave
what's important behind!

1611
01:02:58,483 --> 01:03:00,443
-Let's go save our friends.
-Wet's woll.

1612
01:03:01,277 --> 01:03:02,695
Hey, can I go?

1613
01:03:02,779 --> 01:03:03,905
'Cause if I don't
finish my show,

1614
01:03:03,988 --> 01:03:05,823
- I'm out $600.
- Sir,

1615
01:03:05,907 --> 01:03:06,699
-you need to calm down.
-No, no...

1616
01:03:14,791 --> 01:03:16,209
I know this place.

1617
01:03:16,292 --> 01:03:17,710
We shot an episode
of Love Boat here.

1618
01:03:17,794 --> 01:03:19,003
- Really?
- Here?

1619
01:03:19,086 --> 01:03:20,671
It was
a bottle episode.

1620
01:03:20,755 --> 01:03:22,256
Wait, how old are you?

1621
01:03:22,340 --> 01:03:23,800
You guys hear that?

1622
01:03:23,883 --> 01:03:24,967
- You guys hear that?
- What the heck?

1623
01:03:25,051 --> 01:03:25,635
- Otto!
- Gail! Oh, my God.

1624
01:03:25,718 --> 01:03:27,053
Oh, my God.

1625
01:03:27,136 --> 01:03:28,346
Thank God you're okay.

1626
01:03:28,429 --> 01:03:29,806
I got it.

1627
01:03:30,431 --> 01:03:31,682
Thank you.

1628
01:03:32,433 --> 01:03:33,559
Oh, thank God.

1629
01:03:33,643 --> 01:03:35,228
-Hi. Are you okay?
-Yeah, yeah.

1630
01:03:38,022 --> 01:03:39,816
- Hey.
- Hi.

1631
01:03:46,697 --> 01:03:48,407
My reports, please.

1632
01:03:48,491 --> 01:03:49,951
The reports are...

1633
01:03:50,034 --> 01:03:51,828
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Hold your horses, Slattery.

1634
01:03:51,911 --> 01:03:54,539
Everybody hold your horses.

1635
01:03:54,622 --> 01:03:56,249
We got the reports.
They're close by.

1636
01:03:56,332 --> 01:03:58,000
But first, we're gonna
need some assurance

1637
01:03:58,084 --> 01:03:59,460
that we're getting
out of here alive.

1638
01:03:59,544 --> 01:04:01,879
What? You don't trust me?

1639
01:04:01,963 --> 01:04:03,589
Lady, I trust in
three things only.

1640
01:04:03,673 --> 01:04:05,675
My mommy, death, and taxes.

1641
01:04:05,758 --> 01:04:07,468
And last I checked,
I'm still alive.

1642
01:04:07,552 --> 01:04:09,554
I use TurboTax, and nobody
here's breastfeeding me.

1643
01:04:09,637 --> 01:04:13,432
So, yeah, we got a couple
of requests on our end.

1644
01:04:13,516 --> 01:04:15,768
You are in
no position to bargain.

1645
01:04:15,852 --> 01:04:17,353
We see things
a little bit differently,

1646
01:04:17,436 --> 01:04:19,522
because it seems to us
that without those documents,

1647
01:04:19,605 --> 01:04:21,065
you don't have what you want.

1648
01:04:21,148 --> 01:04:23,109
And it seems to me
that the only people

1649
01:04:23,192 --> 01:04:25,069
who know where
the documents are is us.

1650
01:04:25,152 --> 01:04:28,865
So it seems like right now
you need us alive.

1651
01:04:30,825 --> 01:04:32,076
What do you want?

1652
01:04:32,159 --> 01:04:33,452
You tell your goon boys

1653
01:04:33,536 --> 01:04:34,787
to drop their guns
and leave us alone.

1654
01:04:34,871 --> 01:04:36,372
We walk out of here unscathed.

1655
01:04:36,455 --> 01:04:38,040
You get your documents.
It's a win-win.

1656
01:04:41,836 --> 01:04:44,422
Okay.

1657
01:04:44,505 --> 01:04:46,883
Everybody, put your guns in
the trash and take a break.

1658
01:04:48,634 --> 01:04:49,886
Happy now?

1659
01:04:54,015 --> 01:04:56,142
Well, I feel like they did
everything that we asked for.

1660
01:04:56,225 --> 01:04:57,894
They put
the guns in the trash...

1661
01:04:57,977 --> 01:04:59,645
They gave something,
we need to give something.

1662
01:04:59,729 --> 01:05:00,563
- You guys wanna take a vote?
- Yeah. We all in?

1663
01:05:00,646 --> 01:05:02,064
-Vincent?
-Okay.

1664
01:05:02,148 --> 01:05:02,899
- Give her the reports.
- Yeah.

1665
01:05:05,109 --> 01:05:07,778
Here we go.

1666
01:05:09,488 --> 01:05:10,531
Right there. One more.

1667
01:05:12,617 --> 01:05:14,994
These are... Yeah, right there.
There you are.

1668
01:05:15,077 --> 01:05:16,537
- And we have one more. One more.
- Do you need help?

1669
01:05:16,621 --> 01:05:19,165
-Gail, give me a hand?
-Yeah, sure.

1670
01:05:19,248 --> 01:05:22,793
- Okay.
- Right there. And one more.

1671
01:05:22,877 --> 01:05:24,754
One more. Come on.

1672
01:05:24,837 --> 01:05:26,964
There it is.
And one more, one more.

1673
01:05:34,639 --> 01:05:36,682
Well, that's that.

1674
01:05:36,766 --> 01:05:39,101
-So much for our movie pitch.
-At least we're alive.

1675
01:05:39,185 --> 01:05:40,728
Hey, Caleb, you are
quite a negotiator.

1676
01:05:40,811 --> 01:05:42,188
-Yeah.
-Wow.

1677
01:05:42,271 --> 01:05:43,940
It's all here.

1678
01:05:44,023 --> 01:05:45,191
Hey.

1679
01:05:45,274 --> 01:05:47,777
- Kill them.
- Wait, what?

1680
01:05:47,860 --> 01:05:49,445
Wait, wait, wait...
No, no, no, no, no.

1681
01:05:49,528 --> 01:05:51,030
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

1682
01:05:51,113 --> 01:05:52,740
We should have anticipated
that they'd come back

1683
01:05:52,823 --> 01:05:54,283
and get their guns again.

1684
01:05:54,367 --> 01:05:56,077
Yeah. Don't blame yourself.
I missed it, too.

1685
01:05:56,160 --> 01:05:58,371
These guys are
professional killers, right?

1686
01:05:58,454 --> 01:05:59,664
- We both missed it.
- We all missed it.

1687
01:05:59,747 --> 01:06:01,415
- Yeah.
- I'm kicking myself now.

1688
01:06:01,499 --> 01:06:03,042
It was
right in my face.

1689
01:06:03,125 --> 01:06:04,168
Hey, Slattery,
now would be a good time

1690
01:06:04,251 --> 01:06:05,795
to pull off some
of those moves.

1691
01:06:05,878 --> 01:06:07,046
I told you, I can't...
I can't do it.

1692
01:06:07,129 --> 01:06:08,631
Real violence
makes me throw up.

1693
01:06:08,714 --> 01:06:11,258
John, no flying machine

1694
01:06:11,342 --> 01:06:13,678
will ever fly from
New York to Paris.

1695
01:06:13,761 --> 01:06:17,014
-What?
-Orville Wright said that.

1696
01:06:17,098 --> 01:06:18,432
Now, do you understand
what I'm saying?

1697
01:06:19,100 --> 01:06:20,643
Yeah.

1698
01:06:20,726 --> 01:06:21,936
Yeah, I understand.

1699
01:06:22,937 --> 01:06:24,355
Stand back, everybody.

1700
01:06:24,438 --> 01:06:26,023
- I got this.
- Okay.

1701
01:06:26,107 --> 01:06:27,817
Fellas, fellas.

1702
01:06:27,900 --> 01:06:30,152
Nobody wants to get hurt, right?

1703
01:06:30,236 --> 01:06:31,821
So why don't we just
handle it like this?

1704
01:06:35,741 --> 01:06:36,867
Whoa!

1705
01:06:38,577 --> 01:06:39,870
Hi-yah!

1706
01:06:42,289 --> 01:06:44,000
- Hey, hey, hey.
- Not bad, right?

1707
01:06:45,751 --> 01:06:47,878
Hey, boys. Come on!

1708
01:06:50,339 --> 01:06:51,257
Take that.

1709
01:06:52,383 --> 01:06:54,301
Too slow.

1710
01:06:54,385 --> 01:06:55,886
- Good job.
- Nope.

1711
01:06:59,348 --> 01:07:02,268
What the fuck?

1712
01:07:02,351 --> 01:07:03,561
Consider that a divorce.

1713
01:07:03,644 --> 01:07:04,812
Hey, you're mine!

1714
01:07:04,895 --> 01:07:06,480
You want some,
too, baldy?

1715
01:07:06,564 --> 01:07:08,065
Take that.

1716
01:07:08,149 --> 01:07:11,068
This is fun.
I can do this all day.

1717
01:07:11,152 --> 01:07:12,862
Got your eye, motherfucker.

1718
01:07:12,945 --> 01:07:14,697
Ooh!

1719
01:07:14,780 --> 01:07:16,115
Going up, motherfucker.

1720
01:07:16,198 --> 01:07:17,324
I got you, asshole!

1721
01:07:21,370 --> 01:07:23,122
Down goes Frazier.

1722
01:07:23,205 --> 01:07:24,540
Slattery, you old
son of a bitch.

1723
01:07:26,751 --> 01:07:28,294
Oh! Still got it.

1724
01:07:30,212 --> 01:07:32,506
This is for Nico and Marco

1725
01:07:32,590 --> 01:07:34,175
and all the unnecessary
agita you caused me

1726
01:07:34,258 --> 01:07:35,801
over the last
11 and a half hours.

1727
01:07:35,885 --> 01:07:37,136
-No, no, no, no.
-You kill my friends,

1728
01:07:37,219 --> 01:07:39,346
I kill your friends. Bye-bye.

1729
01:07:39,430 --> 01:07:41,348
No, no, no, no.
Please, please.

1730
01:07:41,432 --> 01:07:43,851
Huh?

1731
01:07:46,228 --> 01:07:48,064
Stings.

1732
01:07:55,404 --> 01:07:57,281
-Whoops.
-Let's face it.

1733
01:07:57,364 --> 01:07:59,116
You can pack quite a punch.
"Let's face it."

1734
01:08:00,868 --> 01:08:02,078
Wow.

1735
01:08:02,161 --> 01:08:03,621
Where did you
learn that, man?

1736
01:08:03,704 --> 01:08:06,248
I'm self-taught.
Totally self-taught.

1737
01:08:06,332 --> 01:08:07,708
I have a practice
head in my garage.

1738
01:08:07,792 --> 01:08:09,001
Did you see that?
He saved my life.

1739
01:08:09,085 --> 01:08:10,544
