but I can do something
for you guys.

1961
01:17:41,657 --> 01:17:44,910
Caleb, what if I was
to call CAA

1962
01:17:44,993 --> 01:17:48,538
and strongly suggest that
they give you your job back?

1963
01:17:48,622 --> 01:17:50,457
-That'd be amazing...
-Yes.

1964
01:17:50,540 --> 01:17:52,250
And, Slattery, I got
roped into doing

1965
01:17:52,334 --> 01:17:54,002
my lawyer's kid's
student film,

1966
01:17:54,086 --> 01:17:56,380
but I bet I could convince them
to give you the job instead.

1967
01:17:56,463 --> 01:17:57,506
Wow. Thanks, man.

1968
01:17:57,589 --> 01:17:58,882
They say that student films

1969
01:17:58,965 --> 01:18:00,217
are the gateway to
bigger stuff sometimes.

1970
01:18:00,300 --> 01:18:01,510
-Vincent?
-Yes?

1971
01:18:01,593 --> 01:18:02,761
You wanted to be a screenwriter?

1972
01:18:03,595 --> 01:18:04,680
Well...

1973
01:18:06,056 --> 01:18:08,767
I'm more of
a photographer these days.

1974
01:18:08,850 --> 01:18:10,394
Would you mind
if I get a shot of you?

1975
01:18:10,477 --> 01:18:11,645
-I'd be honored.
-Yeah!

1976
01:18:11,728 --> 01:18:12,688
Something candid?
Like this?

1977
01:18:15,691 --> 01:18:18,110
